strix-port: ggml's HIP top_k (radix select, ncols > 1024) filled the slots left for values tied AT the k-th threshold
in atomicAdd order, so the selected set was non-deterministic run to run.  Ties now go to the lowest column indices:
the gather counts ties per contiguous block range, top_k_radix_fill_ties ranks them with a block scan in column order.
HIP-only code path (no CUB on HIP); CUDA builds are unchanged.  Apply after xolotl-ggml.patch and strix-01.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/top-k.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/top-k.cu
